# fyr eval Done: review, security and verification, the plan closed; the code-modularity rule (2026-10-26-1112)

Plan: `PLAN-2026-10-26-0659-plan-fyr-eval-the-antigravity-run-kit-as-a-verb`, § Done (D36, D37). Commits ff4c476, e2435b5, 52259a5, 5593cb8, 44df74a, 30c586e, and this record's commit.

## What changed

- Review round 1 over `e49f0b0..c4807c0`:
  - `REVIEW-2026-10-26-1018` (code and docs): 2 low.
  - `REVIEW-2026-10-26-1023` (security): 4 medium, 5 low.
  - Fixed at ff4c476 (D36):
    - an interrupt before the first row writes no record;
    - `evalBody` reads `eval.ProcsChecked`;
    - a sandbox the agent replaced fails `sandbox replaced`, and nothing is removed, run, scanned or ingested through it;
    - check e matches the approved paths;
    - token and settings removal goes through `os.Root`;
    - SIGHUP is caught;
    - check b fails closed;
    - check c also watches `~/.gemini/config` and the CLI's `settings.json`;
    - check d covers the whole sandbox directory;
    - the wrapper refuses an agent's own `--home`;
    - sandbox files are opened `O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK` and must be regular.
  - Rebutted: a sweep for leftover token links, and hashing the check binaries.
  - Left to the operator: containment, the box's Go toolchain, and `metrics.Ingest`'s SQLite parsing.
- Review round 2 over ff4c476 (the cap): `REVIEW-2026-10-26-1040`, code-docs and security. A round-1 fix caused a medium: a fixture's tracked directory link failed every row. The operator chose to fix all with no round 3, and approved the `cmd/fyr/main.go:81` help line. Fixed at 5593cb8 (D37):
  - check d treats a link that the baseline held with the same target as the fixture's, refuses files over 64 MiB, and never follows the sandbox directory itself;
  - an `os.Root` on SB is held from `prepare` to step 14;
  - `prompt2` runs only on an intact sandbox, and a refused output open fails the row;
  - check e runs without the clone;
  - intact is re-tested before check d;
  - check b matches git's full discovery message;
  - the help line is updated.
- `rules/code-modularity.md`, the operator's rule, verbatim, plus a vendored-files exemption approved at the audit (ADR-066, amended). The Antigravity rules block is 20,976 of 22,000 bytes.
- The rule's audit (`.agents/scratch/modularity/`, 15 items) was approved "as plan":
  - item 1: `internal/eval/run.go` (716 lines) is split into six files by whole-declaration moves (52259a5; the sha256 of all 37 declarations is equal);
  - items 2–8 are `PLAN-2026-10-26-modularity`.
- Records: `SPEC-fyr-eval` (steps, checks b–e, failure modes, Known limits), `GUIDE-testing`, BUG-107, BUG-160, plan D36 and D37, and `SPEC-fyr-check` re-read and re-stamped.

## Verification

- Every fix was mutation-checked: its test failed with the fix reverted and passes with it (`.agents/scratch/eval/mut/`, `mut2/`).
- The full suite ran bare: exit 0 at ff4c476 and on the round-2 tree, 12 packages ok.
