# Change — PLAN.md P8: the eval suite's four optional columns (2026-10-31)

Phase: `PLAN.md` P8, item 5 (the eval-metrics plan's Phase 5a). Code commit `e9fad5c`. The checkpoint commit adds the testing record, any re-read stamps and `PLAN.md`'s ticks. ADR-085 supersedes the eval plan's D2 (the seven-column table). The readings where the plan is silent are `PLAN.md` D17.

## What changed

- **The suite grammar** (`internal/eval/suite.go`, new `internal/eval/suite_columns.go`): the header is the seven columns or the seven plus `| version | kind | cluster | expect |`. A row has as many cells as its header. Under the long header:
  - `version`: 1 to 999999999, in plain digits;
  - `kind`: `capability`, `regression`, `adversarial` or `indicator`;
  - `cluster`: one identifier word;
  - `expect`: comma-separated entries, each made of identifier words joined by single spaces, none empty or repeated, at most 120 bytes joined.

  An empty cell gives the default: 1, `capability`, the row's id, none. `Row` gains `Version`, `Kind`, `Cluster` and `Expect`. An id is now at most 64 bytes. The identifier rule is copied from `internal/metrics` (D10: no SQLite driver in `internal/eval`).
- **`fyr eval --list`** (`cmd/fyr/eval.go`): `<id>  <agent or ->  <named or wide>  v<version>  <kind>`. The flag's help text names the two new columns.
- **The trial** (`cmd/fyr/eval_trial.go` `trialOf`, `eval_record.go`): each trial stores its row's version, kind and cluster with the defaults applied, and `expect` or NULL. `internal/metrics/trials.go`'s comment says so.
- **`fyr metrics evals`** (`internal/metrics/evals.go`, `evals_write.go`): a NULL `row_version`, and a session no trial claims, read as version 1, so a row's history does not split now that the default is written. The `v` column prints `1` where it printed `-`.
- **Docs:**
  - `SPEC-fyr-eval`: an Updated line, the `--list` row, § The suite's two headers and four bullets, the id's bound, § Data's trial, § Failure modes' parse row.
  - `SPEC-fyr-metrics`: an Updated line, the schema comment, § Per-row view's version and `--json`, § Data's trial.
  - `GUIDE-eval` § Columns: the four optional columns. The table itself is P9's.
  - `GUIDE-fyr-matrix`: the `--list` row re-exercised, and a `metrics evals` row after P8.
  - `TDD.md` § T13; `PLAN.md` D17.

## Agents dispatched

- `reviewer`, code and docs, round 1 (`REVIEW-2026-10-31-1558-review-plan-md-p8-the-suite-grammar-s-four-colum`): REQUEST CHANGES, with 3 findings, all fixed:
  - the stale `TestEvalListNeedsNoHome` expectation;
  - `SPEC-fyr-metrics`' schema comment;
  - the view's version split, fixed here rather than in P9, and the P9 work described in the present tense.
- `security`, the parser (`REVIEW-2026-10-31-1558-security-plan-md-p8-the-suite-parser-s-four-colu`): CLEAR, with 2 low findings, both fixed:
  - `parseRow`'s evaluation order (no test can fail under gc; D17);
  - the default cluster outrunning the identifier bound, now the 64-byte id.
- `reviewer` round 2 over the fixes (`REVIEW-2026-10-31-1607-review-plan-md-p8-round-2-over-the-fixes-approve`): APPROVE WITH NITS. Its 1 doc nit is fixed. This was the last round.
- `verifier` (`TEST-2026-10-31-1619-verification-plan-md-p8-at-e9fad5c-1821-pass-0-f`): FAIL on `fyr check`'s 7 `spec-stale` findings only (SPEC-fyr-check, -dream, -memory-loop, -record, -search, -serve, -work, untouched by the commit's docs); every Go command passed, every changed function covered. The seven were re-read against `e9fad5c` and stamped in the checkpoint commit; `fyr check` 0 findings.

## Verification

- **Tests first:**
  - `TestSuiteGrammarLong` and `TestSuiteRefusals`' new cases failed to build before `Row`'s fields.
  - `TestEvalVerbList`, `TestEvalVerbListLong` and `TestEvalTrialSuiteFields` failed on the old output and on NULL fields.
  - `TestEvalRowsVersionDefault` failed with `r v0 n2; r v1 n1; r v2 n1`.
  - "an id past 64 bytes" was accepted before the bound.
- **Mutations**, each failing then restored (`.agents/scratch/p8/mutations.txt`):
  - the long header not accepted;
  - `version` as `^[0-9]+$`;
  - `>=` on the 120-byte bound;
  - the bound at 150;
  - `strings.Fields` in place of single spaces;
  - no repeat check;
  - no cluster default;
  - the width check loosened;
  - `Expect` dropped from `trialOf`;
  - the view's NULL default back to 0;
  - the unclaimed session's default removed.
- **Full test command** on the pre-commit tree: exit 0, 15 of 15 packages (`.agents/scratch/p8/full-pre.log`). The verifier's run at `e9fad5c`: exit 0, 1821 pass, 0 fail, 6 skip (P7: 1795); `govulncheck` nothing new; `fyr check` 0 findings after the stamps.
- **`fyr eval --list`** from a tree of this checkout: 63 rows, each `v1  capability`.
- **The eval home** (read only, D27 of the eval-metrics plan), `fyr metrics evals --home ~/sandbox/fyr-eval/home` from a tree binary:
  - 63 rows, every `v` column `1`;
  - the suite line unchanged from P7's E2E (`63 rows graded, 216 graded trials, 2 errors; pass rate 0.98 [0.90, 0.99]`);
  - 0.137 s.

## Not covered

- No real `fyr eval` run under a long-header suite: `GUIDE-eval` keeps seven columns until P9. The long header is exercised through the fake agy in `cmd/fyr`'s tests.
- `parseRow`'s order fix has no test that can fail on gc.
- The per-kind rates, `expect`'s `m of n` and `--list` over the real 63 rows with kinds set are P9's.

