### Extraction order (one file per step; `gofmt -l cmd internal && go vet ./... && go test ./<pkg>` after each, full suite after each package)

1. Smallest risk, pure move: search (5), brain (6), dream/timer (10): rigs first, then clusters.
2. dream: collect_test fixture first (run_test depends on it), then run_test, collect_test; make `fakeagy_test.go` before moving agy tests.
3. eval/run_test (8): move rig, then three test files.
4. cmd/fyr: zip_test (7) rig, then main_test (3) rigs before tests; `isolate`/`checkoutRoot` usage across the two files decides which rig file owns them (compile will say).
5. harness_test (1): repo_test.go first, then clusters from the smallest.
6. catalog_test (2): last; the data and pipe-linter parts are pure moves, `TestRefreshCatalogScript` needs the closure-to-struct rewrite.
After the whole set: re-grep comments naming moved files (eval's three tests cite catalog_test.go), and `go test -count=1 -run 'TestHarnessMap|TestHelper' ./...` to prove the cited and re-exec tests are still found by name.

